guṇā vartanta ity evaṁ
yo ’vatiṣṭhati neṅgate\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":3963,\"bb\":3485,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/14/22-25/b3485/\",\"body_value\":\"sama-duḥkha-sukhaḥ sva-sthaḥ
sama-loṣṭāśma-kāñcanaḥ
tulya-priyāpriyo dhīras
tulya-nindātma-saṁstutiḥ\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":3964,\"bb\":3486,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/14/22-25/b3486/\",\"body_value\":\"mānāpamānayos tulyas
tulyo mitrāri-pakṣayoḥ
sarvārambha-parityāgī
guṇātītaḥ sa ucyate\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":3965,\"bb\":3487,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/14/22-25/b3487/\",\"shadow_value\":\"$25\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"śrī-bhagavān uvāca\",\"translation\":\"the Supreme Personality of Godhead said\"},{\"word\":\"prakāśam\",\"translation\":\"illumination\"},{\"word\":\"ca\",\"translation\":\"and\"},{\"word\":\"pravṛttim\",\"translation\":\"attachment\"},{\"word\":\"ca\",\"translation\":\"and\"},{\"word\":\"moham\",\"translation\":\"illusion\"},{\"word\":\"eva ca\",\"translation\":\"also\"},{\"word\":\"pāṇḍava\",\"translation\":\"O son of Pāṇḍu\"},{\"word\":\"na dveṣṭi\",\"translation\":\"does not hate\"},{\"word\":\"sampravṛttāni\",\"translation\":\"although developed\"},{\"word\":\"na nivṛttāni\",\"translation\":\"nor stopping development\"},{\"word\":\"kāṅkṣati\",\"translation\":\"desires\"},{\"word\":\"udāsīna-vat\",\"translation\":\"as if neutral\"},{\"word\":\"āsīnaḥ\",\"translation\":\"situated\"},{\"word\":\"guṇaiḥ\",\"translation\":\"by the qualities\"},{\"word\":\"yaḥ\",\"translation\":\"one who\"},{\"word\":\"na\",\"translation\":\"never\"},{\"word\":\"vicālyate\",\"translation\":\"is agitated\"},{\"word\":\"guṇāḥ\",\"translation\":\"the qualities\"},{\"word\":\"vartante\",\"translation\":\"are acting\"},{\"word\":\"iti evam\",\"translation\":\"knowing thus\"},{\"word\":\"yaḥ\",\"translation\":\"one who\"},{\"word\":\"avatiṣṭhati\",\"translation\":\"remains\"},{\"word\":\"na\",\"translation\":\"never\"},{\"word\":\"iṅgate\",\"translation\":\"flickers\"},{\"word\":\"sama\",\"translation\":\"equal\"},{\"word\":\"duḥkha\",\"translation\":\"in distress\"},{\"word\":\"sukhaḥ\",\"translation\":\"and happiness\"},{\"word\":\"sva-sthaḥ\",\"translation\":\"being situated in himself\"},{\"word\":\"sama\",\"translation\":\"equally\"},{\"word\":\"loṣṭa\",\"translation\":\"a lump of earth\"},{\"word\":\"aśma\",\"translation\":\"stone\"},{\"word\":\"kāñcanaḥ\",\"translation\":\"gold\"},{\"word\":\"tulya\",\"translation\":\"equally disposed\"},{\"word\":\"priya\",\"translation\":\"to the dear\"},{\"word\":\"apriyaḥ\",\"translation\":\"and the undesirable\"},{\"word\":\"dhīraḥ\",\"translation\":\"steady\"},{\"word\":\"tulya\",\"translation\":\"equal\"},{\"word\":\"nindā\",\"translation\":\"in defamation\"},{\"word\":\"ātma-saṁstutiḥ\",\"translation\":\"and praise of himself\"},{\"word\":\"māna\",\"translation\":\"in honor\"},{\"word\":\"apamānayoḥ\",\"translation\":\"and dishonor\"},{\"word\":\"tulyaḥ\",\"translation\":\"equal\"},{\"word\":\"tulyaḥ\",\"translation\":\"equal\"},{\"word\":\"mitra\",\"translation\":\"of friends\"},{\"word\":\"ari\",\"translation\":\"and enemies\"},{\"word\":\"pakṣayoḥ\",\"translation\":\"to the parties\"},{\"word\":\"sarva\",\"translation\":\"of all\"},{\"word\":\"ārambha\",\"translation\":\"endeavors\"},{\"word\":\"parityāgī\",\"translation\":\"renouncer\"},{\"word\":\"guṇa-atītaḥ\",\"translation\":\"transcendental to the material modes of nature\"},{\"word\":\"saḥ\",\"translation\":\"he\"},{\"word\":\"ucyate\",\"translation\":\"is said to be\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":3966,\"bb\":3488,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/14/22-25/b3488/\",\"body_value\":\"The Supreme Personality of Godhead said: O son of Pāṇḍu, he who does not hate illumination, attachment and delusion when they are present or long for them when they disappear; who is unwavering and undisturbed through all these reactions of the material qualities, remaining neutral and transcendental, knowing that the modes alone are active; who is situated in the self and regards alike happiness and distress; who looks upon a lump of earth, a stone and a piece of gold with an equal eye; who is equal toward the desirable and the undesirable; who is steady,